            <English>Writes build, redraw and frame timings and search and drag costs to the RPT, for FPS reports.\nOff in play.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandDrop">
            <English>Time to drop an item</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandDrop_Desc">
            <English>Seconds the hands are busy dropping one item (drop key, Drop in the menu), one after another.
0 drops at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandEquip">
            <English>Time to put on or take off</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandEquip_Desc">
            <English>Seconds the hands are busy putting one item on or taking it off, for what the switches below let wait.
0 does it at once; a drag never waits.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandMove">
            <English>Time to move to another container</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandMove_Desc">
            <English>Seconds the hands are busy moving one item to another container (quick move, group moves).
0 moves at once; a drag never waits.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide">
            <English>Where other storage opens</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide_Desc">
            <English>Where the column of what you loot opens. Left of my storage: beside it, in the middle of the window.
Right of my storage: at the right edge, and your storage moves aside.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide_Left">
            <English>Left of my storage - my storage stays put</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide_Right">
            <English>Right of my storage - my storage moves aside</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineFillBar">
            <English>Fill bar on magazines</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineFillBar_Desc">
            <English>A thin bar along the bottom of every magazine that is not full, on its tile and on a weapon's magazine slot.\nThe rounds as words have their own switch.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineText">
            <English>Rounds on magazines</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineText_Desc">
            <English>The rounds left in a magazine as words ("17/30") in a corner of its tile; a weapon's slot keeps them.\nOff: the fill bar alone shows how full it is.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MoveToStop">
            <English>Moving stops looting</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MoveToStop_Desc">
            <English>A movement key pressed while looting or searching closes the window and stops the search.\nOff: movement keys do nothing in the window.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PageRows">
            <English>Rows per page of a container</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PageRows_Desc">
            <English>Rows of a tall crate or vehicle shown at a time; taller ones get pages (4 to 39, 10 by default).
0 or 40 shows the whole container. Only for what you loot, not your own gear.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonItems">
            <English>Take and put items</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonItems_Desc">
            <English>Who may take items out of a living person's uniform, vest and backpack, and put items in.\nNobody: the gear can only be looked at.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonNotify">
            <English>Tell the searched player</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonNotify_Desc">
            <English>A player whose gear is opened is told who goes through it; with a backpack on, nearby players hear ACE's zipper.\nOff: only ACE's own backpack interaction still zips.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonOpen">
            <English>Open the whole person</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonOpen_Desc">
            <English>Whose uniform, vest and backpack open with "Inventory" while alive; others open only by the backpack.\nCaptives are surrendered or handcuffed (ACE); the unconscious always open whole.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonWorn">
            <English>Take off worn gear</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonWorn_Desc">
            <English>Who may take off what a living person wears (weapons, helmet, uniform, vest, backpack and the rest).\nCaptives are surrendered or handcuffed (ACE). Bodies can always be stripped.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PlayerColours">
            <English>Players may pick their colours</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PlayerColours_Desc">
            <English>The header gets a palette button: accent, secondary colour, panel colour, transparency.\nOff: everyone sees their Arma colour and the standard look.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchBodies">
            <English>Search bodies</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchBodies_Desc">
            <English>What a body carries stays a sealed "Unsearched" box until it has been searched - also once dropped.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchContainers">
            <English>Search crates and vehicles</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchContainers_Desc">
            <English>What a crate or a vehicle holds stays a sealed "Unsearched" box until it has been searched.\nSingle objects can be skipped: Eden "Skip searching", Zeus right click, or [_box, false] call einv_gui_fnc_setSearchable;</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchGround">
            <English>Search the ground</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchGround_Desc">
            <English>A pile on the ground stays a sealed "Unsearched" box until it has been searched.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchOnClick">
            <English>Search starts on click</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchOnClick_Desc">
            <English>A box is searched once its Search button is clicked; several boxes can search at the same time.\nOff: every box starts searching by itself.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchPersons">
            <English>Search living persons</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchPersons_Desc">
            <English>What a living person carries stays sealed until searched, awake, unconscious or captive.\nBodies follow "Search bodies".</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTime">
            <English>Search time per cell</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeBackpack">
            <English>Search time: backpacks</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeBackpack_Desc">
            <English>Times the search time per cell for a backpack, worn or lying anywhere: 1 the same, 2 twice as long.\n0 shows a backpack's contents at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeBody">
            <English>Search time: bodies</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeBody_Desc">
            <English>Times the time of a body's uniform, vest and backpack on top of their own factor, also once dropped.\n1 the same, 2 twice as long, 0 shows what a body carries at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeCrate">
            <English>Search time: crates</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeCrate_Desc">
            <English>Times the search time per cell for a crate or box: 1 the same, 2 twice as long.\n0 shows a crate's contents at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeGround">
            <English>Search time: ground</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeGround_Desc">
            <English>Times the search time per cell for a pile on the ground (needs "Search the ground"): 1 the same.\n0 shows the ground at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeUniform">
            <English>Search time: uniforms</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeUniform_Desc">
            <English>Times the search time per cell for a uniform's pockets, worn or lying anywhere: 1 the same, 2 twice as long.\n0 shows a uniform's contents at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeVehicle">
            <English>Search time: vehicles</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeVehicle_Desc">
            <English>Times the search time per cell for a vehicle's cargo, also while you sit in it: 1 the same, 2 twice as long.\n0 shows a vehicle's cargo at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeVest">
            <English>Search time: vests</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTimeVest_Desc">
            <English>Times the search time per cell for a vest, worn or lying anywhere: 1 the same, 2 twice as long.\n0 shows a vest's contents at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTime_Desc">
            <English>Seconds it takes to search one grid cell of loot; a 2x2 item takes four times as long.\n0 shows everything at once. Each kind of box below can take longer or shorter.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchZeus">
            <English>Search Zeus-placed crates and vehicles</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchZeus_Desc">
            <English>Crates and vehicles placed with Zeus are searched like any other.\nOff: they show their loot at once. Needs "Search crates and vehicles" on.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_ShowNearby">
            <English>Show everything nearby</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_ShowNearby_Desc">
            <English>Shows every pile on the ground and crate within reach as a box in the loot column, nearest first.\nOff: only what you opened shows, as in the vanilla inventory.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SoundsWorld">
            <English>Others hear looting</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SoundsWorld_Desc">
            <English>Players nearby hear someone loot (searching, a rifle taken, a backpack dropped, a reload), up to 10 to 20 m.\nOff: only the looter hears anything.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_TileNames">
            <English>Item names on tiles</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_TileNames_Desc">
            <English>The item's short name in the top right corner of every tile; the Arsenal's panel follows.\nOff: the picture alone, the name still shows at the mouse.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitDrop">
            <English>Dropping waits</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitDrop_Desc">
            <English>Whether the drop key and Drop in the menu take the hands' time (time to drop an item).
Off drops at once; a drag never waits.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitEquip">
            <English>Equipping other items waits</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitEquip_Desc">
            <English>Whether putting on and taking off other items (goggles, night vision, binoculars, weapon parts) takes the hands' time.
Off does it at once; a drag never waits.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitMove">
            <English>Quick move waits</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitMove_Desc">
            <English>Whether the quick move, a double click and a group quick move take the hands' time.
Off moves them at once; a drag never waits.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitWorn">
            <English>Uniform, vest, backpack and helmet wait</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_WaitWorn_Desc">
            <English>Whether putting on and taking off a uniform, vest, backpack or headgear takes the hands' time.
Off does it at once; a drag never waits.</English>
        </Key>
